<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">jcb</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2064712</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">20060611320061128c</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1083/jcb.20060611320061128c</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></article-categories><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Nickerson</surname><given-names>Daniel P.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>West</surname><given-names>Matthew</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Odorizzi</surname><given-names>Greg</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>18</day><month>12</month><year>2006</year></pub-date><volume>175</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>1043</fpage><lpage>1043</lpage><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2006, The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2006</copyright-year><self-uri xlink:title="pdf" xlink:href="jcb1751043.pdf"/></article-meta></front><body><p>Vol. 175 No. 5, December 4, 2006. Pages <related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="175" page="715" id="N0x8c70ac0N0x8b40128" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="17130288" ext-link-type="pubmed">715&#x02013;720</related-article>.</p><p>An incorrect citation appeared in the final paragraph of the Introduction. The corrected sentence, along with full bibliographic information for the correct citation, appears below.</p><p>We report that Did2, a protein related to ESCRT-III subunits (Amerik et al., 2000), directs Vps4 activity to the dissociation of ESCRT-III.</p><p>Amerik, A.Y., J. Nowak, S. Swaminathan, and M. Hochstrasser. 2000. The Doa4 deubiquitinating enzyme is functionally linked to vacuolar protein-sorting and endocytic pathways. <italic>Mol. Biol. Cell.</italic> 11:3365&#x02013;3380.</p><p>Note that the html and pdf versions of this article have been corrected. The error remains only in the print version.</p></body></article>